 like there will be any cases where unbound generic types are passed into this function, since they can only be used in typeof expressions. I'm not sure.\r\nIs there any better solution?","created_at":"2025-03-21T15:57:26Z","updated_at":"2025-03-22T09:37:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104279#discussion_r2007875583","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104279","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2007875583"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104279#discussion_r2007875583"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104279"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2007875583/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":186,"original_line":186,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2006238217,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"}]